# build & run artifacts
harness/run/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# local audio renders / scratch
#
# `*.wav` USED TO BE BLANKET AND IT ATE REAL SOURCE. The rule was written for
# render artifacts, but git applies it to everything: twenty Amen sample WAVs
# were "on main" from where the user was sitting and had never been committed at
# all, because `git add` skips an ignored file SILENTLY -- no error, no warning,
# nothing in `git status`. The same shape as every other bug in this repo: a
# rule that is correct about the case it was written for and wrong about the
# case nobody checked.
#
# So the ignore now names the places renders actually land, and anything under
# `samples/` is source and is kept. If you add a new render directory, add it
# here rather than reaching for a wildcard.
/*.wav
harness/**/*.wav
!samples/**
scratch/
.DS_Store
# output-test renders (harness/test_output.js): WAVs plus their manifest.json --
# regenerated on every run, never source
harness/output_renders*/

# editor / tooling
.claude/

# npm dependencies. These were swept into a composition commit (4a4dbc8) by a
# broad `git add` and stayed tracked for months -- 176 files nobody meant to
# commit. `npm install` restores them; the browser is already on the image at
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH, so no download is needed.
node_modules/
